(OMFS distinguishes ordinary allocation blocks from system blocks carrying) Tj
T* (metadata. They share the same block-address namespace, even if the metadata) Tj
T* (object uses fewer bytes than an allocated data block. A physical allocation) Tj
T* (address is multiplied by the normal block size, not the smaller system-record) Tj
T* (size. Unused space in a smaller system block is not a separate free) Tj
T* (allocation. The known device profiles commonly use 2048 to 8192-byte blocks;) Tj
T* (independently verify each supported block-size and mirror configuration.) Tj
T* (Bound the partition offset, address and length before reading. Metadata and) Tj
T* (allocation fields are stored big-endian.) Tj
